WEBVTT

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:05.560
A trespasser?

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.560
Forget about trespassers.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.530
Find the Beast now!

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:14.200
We shall slay the fiend and present
its corpse before His Majesty!

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.620
What the devil's this?

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:20.160
We saw the Beast slaughter them yesterday!

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.410
What the hell's happening?!

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:24.790
I think I understand.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.210
It's a time loop.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:28.880
And I know the malnomen.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:33.050
This is a closed world
created by a curse-bearer.

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:35.050
Chloé.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.400
Wow! I didn't know
that thing could do that!

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:49.230
Vanitas?!

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:52.070
All right, let's head
straight for the castle!

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:54.530
Don't be a fool. Get off!

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:56.820
I'm going to slay the Beast!

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:59.780
I know. And I'm going
to save the curse-bearer.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:02.240
I repaid my debt to you.
If you persist in--

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:03.790
Are you sure?

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:06.710
This is what you wish?

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:09.210
I am a bourreau.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:13.920
I must not cause any further trouble
for Master Luca and Lord Ruthven.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.130
Whoa!

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:26.980
Now then, where could that fool be?

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:54.230
"The Case Study of Vanitas"

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.280
Wh-What was that shaking?

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:08.370
It's finally starting to work.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:12.170
You put something in my food?

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:15.000
Jean-Jacques?

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:21.800
I'll likely try to kill you if you
keep getting in Chloé's way.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:25.390
So sleep it off here
until the coast is clear.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:32.480
Chloé told me.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:37.070
You're not just a vampire.
You can also read memories via blood.

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:39.360
When I heard that, I had a thought.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.400
A wish, if you will.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:46.030
I wish for someone to remember us.
Even one person will do.

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:48.790
No. Please, wait.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:50.120
I'm sorry.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.180
Hmph!

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.720
Bring me my booze!

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:19.150
Is this one of Jean's memories?

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:23.990
Enough!

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.040
Who are you?

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.250
Oh, um...

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:35.120
My name's Jean.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:38.170
Jean-Jacques Chastel.

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:42.590
A-Are you... the Silver Witch?

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:46.760
My grandma and grandpa
told me stories about you,

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:51.430
the little silver-haired witch
who appears in the forest.

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:53.770
I was wondering...

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:56.730
Eyes of red. Are you a vampire?

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.400
N-No, I'm...

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:11.490
Are you... just like me?

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.920
Another victim?

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:22.550
How horrible. How many dozens
of deaths does that make so far?

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:24.920
Someone claims to have seen a huge beast.

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:32.100
Rumor has it that Marquis d'Apchier has
long been meddling in uncanny research.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:37.650
I heard his research is what created
the Silver Witch who haunts the forest.

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:40.440
They say the Beast is her familiar!

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:45.030
No! The Beast of Gévaudan is
none other than the witch herself!

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:47.700
No! It's not Chloé!

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:53.580
She's trying to protect you all by
discovering the Beast's true identity!

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:58.170
The Beast slew the marquis and his son.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:02.800
Then the marquis's wife took her own life.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:07.130
They're all dead because of me.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:11.180
The d'Apchiers are gone
because they sheltered a vampire.

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:12.850
I was told...

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:16.060
...that I'm a monster.

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:20.190
You need not worry, Chloé.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:22.770
You've done nothing wrong.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:27.240
I'll stay by your side forever.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:46.670
If only I were more powerful...

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:54.260
Did you hear?

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:58.480
A Chasseur and the Senate's bourreau
are here to hunt down the Beast.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:01.350
The Beast has seen its final day!

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:10.530
Kill!

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:11.910
Kill the witch!

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:14.030
Kill the Beast of Gévaudan!

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:16.950
Kill!

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:24.540
Chloé was the only one
who would protect me.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:27.710
The only one who needed me.

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:30.800
It is for her sake...

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:32.090
I must...

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:35.720
I must become far more powerful!

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:37.640
I must!

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:53.070
Jean-Jacques.

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:56.330
He's the Beast of Gévaudan.

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:02.580
Jean-Jacques, do you loathe this world?

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:04.330
I do.

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:09.000
I loathe the humans who scorn Chloé
and the vampires who abandoned her.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:10.880
I'll devour them all.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:13.550
This I vow.

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:25.190
What could that be?

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:31.820
It's Jean-Jacques.

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:34.450
He's such a kind boy, isn't he?

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:39.740
He gave me his pristine true name
in order to protect you.

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:43.370
After all, the only way to prove
that you're not the Beast

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:47.540
is for someone else to take its form.

00:08:57.390 --> 00:09:00.140
You must flee, Chloé.

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:03.350
The Senate's bourreau...

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:06.650
...and the Hellfire Witch are after you.

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:08.400
The Senate?

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:12.570
August?

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:34.920
Jeanne.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:43.020
So you're... the Hellfire Witch?

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.780
I'm so glad.

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:01.080
You finally returned for me.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.500
Go on, quickly now.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:06.710
There isn't much time.

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:11.630
Use your fangs, your talons,
your flames, and...

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:14.630
Well? Come on.

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:16.170
Quickly now!

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:34.320
I'll look forward to the day when
I can see how you've grown, Jeanne.

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:43.410
No. W-Wait!

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.410
Chloé!

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:56.800
I can make peace with this. I can.

00:10:56.800 --> 00:11:00.800
Forgive me, Jean-Jacques.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:03.430
Are you sure about this?

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:10.020
Poor little Chloé.

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:12.560
You've done nothing wrong.

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:17.610
Yet the vampires and humans
have cast you away like rubbish.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:19.280
Aren't you sad?

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:21.530
Aren't you bitter?

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:26.740
You don't wish to take
vengeance upon Gévaudan?

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:29.460
Yes, I'm bitter.

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:33.500
I will never ever forgive them.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:35.920
I <i>will</i> have my vengeance!

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:49.060
Commence

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:50.770
calculation.

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:20.050
Chloé, do you know what I think?

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:24.680
Perhaps the Beast isn't even real.

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:29.060
Everyone is just terrified
for no good reason.

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:35.810
The hunt won't end
until the Beast is dead.

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:41.190
So I shall assume
the form you hunters seek!

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:45.200
Now, try to slay me if you can!

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:49.240
Slay me before I devour
every last one of you!

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:57.790
Father?

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:00.960
You were trouble enough
when you were a vampire.

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:04.090
And now I find you're the Beast.

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:09.180
But I can claim
a fine reward if I kill you.

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:14.390
You've proven yourself useful for
something in the end, Jean-Jacques!

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:22.860
It hurts.

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:25.610
Such terrible pain.

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:27.700
Help...

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:30.080
Somebody, please...

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:33.660
Light. I see light.

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:39.250
Hey.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:43.380
Why are you about to kick
the bucket again, Noé?

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:47.840
Vanitas.

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:51.470
Is it truly you?

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:53.390
Is it?

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:56.140
Does this hurt?

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:57.230
Yes.

00:13:57.230 --> 00:13:59.190
Welcome back to reality.

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:00.310
Thanks.

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:02.690
What the devil happened to you?

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:04.570
Someone slip you some bad medicine?

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:08.410
Yes, it would appear so.

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:10.450
Wait, seriously?

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:12.700
Are Dante and Jeanne with you?

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:13.790
Yes.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:14.790
Is everyone okay?

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:16.160
Yes.

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:18.750
What a relief. I was so worried.

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:22.880
<i>You</i> were worried?! What about <i>me</i>?!

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:23.920
What?

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:24.960
Never mind!

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:25.800
What?

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:27.260
Enough about that!

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:31.760
Did you learn anything useful
while you were in the castle?

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:33.220
Youch!

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:36.640
Jeanne said Chloé d'Apchier is the Beast.

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:39.270
No! That's not true.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:55.040
I see. The man you call
Jean-Jacques is the Beast.

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:59.500
And Chloé is a vampire who
willingly became a curse-bearer.

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:00.620
That's right.

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:06.050
However, they haven't killed
a single soul as far as I've seen.

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:10.220
Then this has all been in vain.

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:12.260
Her motive was vengeance?

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:17.270
Well, there is no need to treat her
if she became a curse-bearer willingly.

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:21.100
No! You can't simply leave her like this!

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:22.690
Why not?

00:15:22.690 --> 00:15:25.440
Vengeance is meaningless,
so she should stop?

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:27.780
Or it won't bring happiness for anyone?

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:29.490
Is that what you wish to say?

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:33.570
Vengeance!

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:37.410
No! That's not what I'm saying, Vanitas.

00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:41.000
I still don't know what
is inside Chloé's head.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.500
I don't know what she truly seeks.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:46.960
I don't even know what
salvation would be for them.

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:50.550
I don't wish to leave here
without discovering what that is!

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:58.470
Well, I do have to recover
<i>The Book of Vanitas</i>.

00:15:58.470 --> 00:15:59.310
What?

00:15:59.310 --> 00:16:02.600
I'll join you until then.

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:04.810
You truly <i>are</i> dim.

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:12.660
I'm saying I'll work with you
until you're satisfied.

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:17.160
If you wish for me to treat them,
try to inspire my help.

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:19.620
Very well! I'll do my best!

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:21.040
Lower your voice!

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:29.210
If Jean-Jacques became
the Beast to protect Chloé,

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:33.300
then who or what is behind
the killings that took place before that?

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:37.760
Local superstitions are
yet strong here in Gévaudan.

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:40.220
There are many religious sects as well,

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:45.100
and vampires are seen as abominations
worthy of hatred and extermination.

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:48.110
Extermination? You mean...

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:49.610
Vampire hunting?

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:53.610
At the time, the war between humans
and vampires had already ended.

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:56.570
Vampire hunting was
no longer officially sanctioned.

00:16:56.570 --> 00:17:00.330
As such, they needed a proxy.

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:05.330
What if a wild animal came out of nowhere

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:08.960
to devour the bodies of
those purged from the Church?

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:11.340
Are you saying they exploited that?

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:13.300
This is mere speculation.

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:19.930
But the bishop at the time pronounced,
"The Beast is a servant of God."

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:23.520
So it was the Church that
created the Beast legend?

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:27.560
And they are also behind the
human slaughter in Gévaudan?

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:29.820
Well, well!

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:32.690
You, too, survived unscathed.

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:34.240
How unfortunate.

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:35.280
Astolfo!

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:36.820
Speak of the devil.

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:40.870
Are you here to destroy the
evidence from a century past?!

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:50.460
Please go on ahead, Vanitas.

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:52.340
This one's mine!

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:57.220
Clobber him once really good for me.

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:18.910
I see. That keyboard controls
the engine's many devices.

00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:23.700
Chloé d'Apchier, I presume?

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:25.330
And you are?

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:30.130
My name is Vanitas,
doctor and vampire specialist.

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:31.750
Fear not.

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:35.260
I've come to save you, or so I intend.

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:36.590
Therefore,

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:39.760
I would have you return
my book this instant!

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:42.220
What book?

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:43.600
My book!

00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:46.810
The one with the black pages
and blue leather cover!

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:49.600
Oh, that one.

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:52.020
It's here somewhere.

00:18:53.270 --> 00:18:54.530
Quoi?

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:57.990
I was curious about the
jewel inlaid upon its cover.

00:18:57.990 --> 00:19:01.990
But try as I might, I failed to remove it,
so I just left it lying around.

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:05.290
I vaguely remember Jean-Jacques
putting it away somewhere.

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:06.830
Oh no!

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:10.420
Don't tell me you're another
spatially challenged vampire?!

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:13.420
I didn't lose it. I put it down somewhere!

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:17.460
And? I heard you say you would save me.

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:21.470
Are you friend or foe? Which do you claim?

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:24.140
Chloé.

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:27.770
He is your foe, your enemy.

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:32.150
And I hate him. I truly do.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:34.690
I'm nobody's friend.

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:38.610
I'll leave the boy's partner to you.

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:43.200
Very well!

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:46.370
Chloé d'Apchier!

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:49.500
What will you rewrite
with the Alteration Engine?!

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:52.290
For what do you seek vengeance?!

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:59.970
Analysis complete.

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:02.720
Coordinates set.

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:12.060
Chloé is going to erase Gévaudan
from the face of the earth!

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:14.230
Completely! Utterly!

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:17.860
People, animals, forests,
mountains, everything!

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:22.070
They'll all be cast away into oblivion!

00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:26.160
I wonder what's in store.

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:29.870
I can't wait to see this!

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:32.670
She's not merely tampering
with the World Formula?

00:20:32.670 --> 00:20:34.880
She's erasing part of it?

00:20:34.880 --> 00:20:40.130
Erasing an area as large as Gévaudan
will have vast repercussions.

00:20:40.130 --> 00:20:43.050
Chloé d'Apchier! Don't do this!

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:51.270
Wait a moment.

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:54.270
Could it be she seeks to...?

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:55.940
Definitions changed.

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:57.360
Alter phenomenon.

00:20:57.360 --> 00:21:00.530
No! Don't activate that engine!

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:02.990
Perpetuate existence.

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:16.460
Wh-What's this?

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:32.310
She has forced Naenia
to take a bodily form!

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:36.520
I've thought about this ever so long.

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:41.190
How could I end this perpetual nightmare?

00:21:41.190 --> 00:21:45.950
How could I lay hands
upon this incorporeal thing?

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:53.000
At last.

00:21:54.460 --> 00:21:57.790
Now, even I could slay you.

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:05.090
"The Beast"

00:23:36.830 --> 00:23:41.580
"Hands Upon a Nightmare"
